# Browsers we support. Low-end Android and old iPads are the real floor for this
# audience, so the baseline is deliberately far below "modern evergreen".
#
# Keep this the ONLY browserslist source. Adding a `browserslist` key to
# package.json as well makes the build fail outright:
#   "contains both .browserslistrc and package.json with browsers".
#
# IMPORTANT — what this does and does not protect against:
#   It lowers SYNTAX (optional chaining, class fields, async generators…).
#   It does NOT lower runtime features baked into a regex literal. Regex
#   LOOKBEHIND `(?<=…)` is a parse-time SyntaxError on Safari < 16.4 and no
#   transpiler can rewrite it. That is what crashed the whole app on iOS 15:
#   react-markdown pulled in `mdast-util-gfm-autolink-literal`, which ships one.
#   Markdown is now rendered by src/lib/markdown, which is lookbehind-free.
#   Before adding any browser dependency, grep it for `(?<=` and `(?<!`.
iOS >= 12
Safari >= 12
Chrome >= 80
Firefox >= 78
Edge >= 88
not dead
not op_mini all
